# Q1: Sorting Algorithms
## 1. Selection Sort
**Pseudocode:**
ALGORITHM SelectionSort(data)
    arr ← COPY(data)
    comparisons ← 0
    swaps ← 0
    FOR i ← 0 TO LENGTH(arr) - 1
        min_index ← i
        FOR j ← i + 1 TO LENGTH(arr) - 1
            comparisons ← comparisons + 1
            IF arr[j] < arr[min_index] THEN
                min_index ← j
            END IF
        END FOR
        IF min_index ≠ i THEN
            SWAP arr[i] AND arr[min_index]
            swaps ← swaps + 1
        END IF
    END FOR
    RETURN arr, comparisons, swaps
END ALGORITHM
## 2. Bubble Sort
**Pseudocode:**
ALGORITHM BubbleSort(data)
    arr ← COPY(data)
    comparisons ← 0
    swaps ← 0
    FOR i ← 0 TO LENGTH(arr) - 1
        swapped ← FALSE
        FOR j ← 0 TO LENGTH(arr) - i - 2
            comparisons ← comparisons + 1
            IF arr[j] > arr[j + 1] THEN
                SWAP arr[j] AND arr[j + 1]
                swaps ← swaps + 1
                swapped ← TRUE
            END IF
        END FOR
        IF swapped = FALSE THEN
            BREAK
        END IF
    END FOR
    RETURN arr, comparisons, swaps
END ALGORITHM
## 3. Insertion Sort
**Pseudocode:**
ALGORITHM InsertionSort(data)
    arr ← COPY(data)
    comparisons ← 0
    movements ← 0
    FOR i ← 1 TO LENGTH(arr) - 1
        key ← arr[i]
        j ← i - 1
        WHILE j ≥ 0
            comparisons ← comparisons + 1
            IF arr[j] > key THEN
                arr[j + 1] ← arr[j]
                movements ← movements + 1
                j ← j - 1
            ELSE
                BREAK
            END IF
        END WHILE
        arr[j + 1] ← key
        movements ← movements + 1
    END FOR
    RETURN arr, comparisons, movements
END ALGORITHM
## 4. Generate Test Datasets
**Pseudocode:**
ALGORITHM GenerateDatasets
    SET random seed to 42
    CREATE Already Sorted dataset
        VALUES from 1 to 100
    CREATE Reverse Sorted dataset
        VALUES from 100 down to 1
    CREATE Random Data dataset
        SELECT 100 unique random numbers
        FROM the range 1 to 1000
    CREATE Nearly Sorted dataset
        COPY the Already Sorted dataset
    REPEAT 5 TIMES
        SELECT two random positions
        SWAP the values at those positions
    END REPEAT
    RETURN all four datasets
END ALGORITHM
## 5. Main Program
**Pseudocode:**
ALGORITHM Main
    datasets ← GenerateDatasets()
    algorithms ←
        Selection Sort
        Bubble Sort
        Insertion Sort
    FOR EACH dataset IN datasets
        DISPLAY dataset name
        DISPLAY input size
        FOR EACH algorithm IN algorithms
            START execution timer
            result, comparisons, movements, elapsed
                ← EXECUTE algorithm(dataset)
            STOP execution timer
            CHECK whether result equals sorted dataset
            DISPLAY algorithm name
            DISPLAY comparisons
            DISPLAY swaps or movements
            DISPLAY execution time
            DISPLAY sorting correctness
        END FOR
    END FOR
END ALGORITHM